{
  "rationale": "The plant is split into sensing and motion capability. The specifications implement a conservative exploration policy with one-shot action states, obstacle-triggered recovery, rare backward escape only for front blockage, directed turning for side obstacles, and a last-resort full rotation only after repeated front-blocked recovery failure. Action states self-loop on path_clear to respect the runtime rule that noncritical uncontrollable events should not preempt the intended pulse, while obstacle events force safe recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Use separate plant automata for sensor outcomes and motion commands so the supervisor can compose perception with action constraints cleanly.",
    "Use a small set of specification automata: one main policy automaton plus lightweight anti-repetition automata to prevent endless turning or random-walk repetition while preserving strong forward bias."
  ],
